# No upper bound on websockets, on purpose: this file only feeds eval.lock.txt, and every version
# in that lock must equal the CI pin (tests/unit/train/test_envs.py). A new websockets therefore
# reaches the eval tier only by moving the CI pin, and the CI test job then runs both shipped
# clients -- check-server and openpi-client's WebsocketClientPolicy (the bench-eval client) --
# against the reference and in-process servers on it. websockets 17.1 deprecated the bare
# connect() openpi-client still calls: check that call before moving the pin to a new major.
